185 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 526 0 R
/E (Scarcity: ETH's issuance is capped at roughly 1.5% annually, and its burn mechanism actively destroys ETH in proportion to network usage, making the effective supply potentially deflationary. Unlike gold, where a sustained price increase could incentivize more mining, ETH's issuance rate is fixed by protocol regardless of price, and its burn rate actually increases with demand.)
/Pg 15 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
